NOT DISTRIBUTED WITH THIS PACKAGE
---------------------------------
cnc-ddraw (MIT, (c) github.com/FunkyFr3sh) is REQUIRED and is not included
either. Diablo II 1.10's own DirectDraw does not initialise on modern Windows,
so the game cannot start without a wrapper. It is MIT and could have been
shipped; it is not, because this project distributes nobody else's binaries.
The launcher looks for it, adopts one from the player's own Diablo II folder if
it is there, and refuses to start with instructions if it is not.
Get it from https://github.com/FunkyFr3sh/cnc-ddraw

Earlier versions of this package also contained d2gl (GPL-3.0), SlashGaming
Diablo II Free Resolution (AGPL-3.0-or-later) and DSOAL (LGPL-2.1). Bundling
them was a mistake: distributing a copyleft program in the same package as this
one raises obligations that this project cannot honour, and the question of how
far those obligations reach is not one to settle by guessing.

They are optional graphics and sound add-ons, not part of the mod. They are no
longer distributed here. The README explains what each one does, where to
download it from its own author, and how to install it -- the same way the
player already supplies their own copy of Diablo II. The game runs without
them.

